#!/bin/sh
# KitchenPC browser launcher. 2026-11-02: Microsoft Edge, because Sling refused Brave on Linux and named
# Chrome or Edge. GPU stays off by policy in /etc/opt/edge/policies/managed (#205).
# --enable-unsafe-swiftshader: WebGL on the CPU. Without it the Windy radar on WEATHER throws a modal
# "radar failed" box that blocks the whole panel, including the app's X.
# --force-renderer-accessibility: 2026-11-08 Jeff: "Make sure the key board is popping up when I need to enter
# text it wouldn't come up when I tryed to log in to sling". The on-screen keyboard (Onboard, auto-show) only
# pops up when the browser ANNOUNCES the focused text box over AT-SPI; Edge does not reliably do that unless
# forced. PROVEN on Sling's real sign-in page 11-08 ~8:42 AM, same fresh profile + window, only this flag
# changed: WITHOUT it the tap put the cursor in the Email box (a typed 'z' landed there) and NO keyboard came
# up at 1/2/4 s; WITH it the 1920x171 keyboard was up in 1 s. (A plain local test page popped the keyboard
# even without the flag - that is why osk-test.sh also checks the running Edge carries the flag.)
# Flags only count when THIS launcher starts the Edge process (the kiosk does, at login); later windows join
# it. ~/.local/share/applications/microsoft-edge.desktop points the menu entry here too.
# --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required: 2026-11-08, Fox News at 6 AM (hcc-fox-news) must start WITH
# sound and nobody standing there to tap.
# --load-extension=~/.local/share/hcc/sling-streamauth: 2026-11-11, THE FIX FOR SLING 7-403 (#281).
# Read out of Sling's own bundle: isStreamAuthEnabled(){return getLDFlagStatus("use-stream-authoriser")||window.enableStreamAuth}
# Sling ships use-streamauth-qvt ON (so loadTimeline SKIPS downloadQVT and expects the QVT inside the
# stream-auth response) while use-stream-authoriser is OFF (so that response is {ssai_manifest:null} with
# no .qvt at all). filterQvt(undefined) then throws "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading
# 'playback_info')", which Sling mislabels as 7-403 - which is why NO qvt request ever left this box
# while curl fetched the same URL fine. The extension sets that global before any Sling code runs.
# PROVEN 11-11 12:09 on Xvfb :77: <video> 1280x720, readyState 4, currentTime advanced 35 s over 35 s,
# zero 7-403 lines, Fox News 'America Reports' on screen. Flags only count for the Edge process THIS
# launcher starts (the kiosk, at login) - later windows join it.
# --user-data-dir + --remote-debugging-port: 2026-11-11, so the kiosk's buttons can be pressed with a
# REAL mouse event inside the page (hcc-cdp-click) instead of an xdotool tap at screen coordinates.
# WHY: hcc-fox-news tapped pixels whose position it had measured BEFORE fullscreen was applied, and
# applying fullscreen moves the window ~20 px - WATCH NOW sat at (192,521) un-maximized but (172,501)
# fullscreen. Measured 11-11 17:04: a mis-landed tap hit the red REC dot and started an unwanted DVR
# recording while the log printed "tapped prompt /^WATCH NOW$/" and nothing played. A CDP event uses
# the element's own viewport rect, so the window's position on screen cannot make it miss.
# Edge 136+ REFUSES --remote-debugging-port on the DEFAULT profile dir, which is why this is its own
# directory. It was copied from the default profile on 11-11 and carries Jeff's Sling sign-in; from
# here on this IS the kiosk's profile, so anything signed into on the kitchen screen lives here.
# The port listens on 127.0.0.1 only. PROVEN 11-11: Fox News playing, currentTime advancing, one
# uncorked Edge sink-input, plus a channel change and a DVR recording played the same way.
exec microsoft-edge --no-first-run --password-store=basic --enable-unsafe-swiftshader --force-renderer-accessibility --autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required --load-extension="$HOME/.local/share/hcc/sling-streamauth" --user-data-dir="$HOME/.local/share/hcc/edge-kiosk" --remote-debugging-port=9222 "$@"
